>> title: Campechanas
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: pastry, sugar, mexican, laminated, oven
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: campechana, campechanas, campechanas de azúcar, campechanas de azucar, sugar glazed puff pastry, shattering pastry
>> pairs-with: hojaldre, orejas
>> servings: 18
>> time: 1 hr 20 min

>> step: roll thin on sugar
Roll @hojaldre{750%g}(three-quarters of a batch, cold) as thin as it will go — you should read print through it — on a bench dusted with @granulated sugar{1%cup}(200 g).

>> step: grease, roll to a rope, coil 18, chill 30 min
Brush @&(~1)thin sheet{} with @melted lard{2%Tbs}(28 g), roll it up into a tight rope from the long side, cut 18 lengths, stand each on its cut end, and ~chill{30%min}.

>> step: flatten into sugar
Flatten @&(~1)coils{} with a rolling pin into thin ovals, pressing them into @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g) as you go until they are wider than your hand and coated on both sides.

>> step: bake at 400°F 15 min
Bake @&(~1)flattened coils{} at 400°F for ~bake{15%min}, until the sugar has run to a pale amber glass over the leaves.
